---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, appStoreUrl } from '../lib/site';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Press', url: '/press/' }];
---
<Base
  title="Inkline press kit: boilerplate, facts and assets | Inkline"
  description="Press information for Inkline: boilerplate, dated factual claims, founder details and downloadable assets."
  path="/press/"
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <div slot="masthead">
  <p class="kicker">Press</p>
  <h1>Press kit</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Boilerplate</h2>
    <p>{SITE.boilerplate}</p>

    <h2>Facts, with dates</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Launched on the App Store in July 2026 as an iPhone and iPad app.</li>
      <li>Source registry of 817 publications across 55 markets and 34 languages, hand-picked and feed-verified; registry v1, updated 17 July 2026.</li>
      <li>Version 1.2, "The Editorial Update", added the publication directory, unified search, the Voices newsroom directory and coverage comparison.</li>
      <li>Free to use; Inkline Pro from £2.99 a month or £14.99 a year in the UK, each with a week free. No accounts, no server-side component.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Founder</h2>
    <p>{SITE.author.name}, {SITE.author.title} and Wikipedia editor. Contact for interviews: <a href="mailto:hello@inklinenews.com">hello@inklinenews.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>Assets</h2>
    <p>The downloadable zip of the Inkdrop mark, app icon and native-resolution screenshots is placed here from the §11.1 brand handover. Until the handover lands, asset requests to <a href="mailto:hello@inklinenews.com">hello@inklinenews.com</a> are answered by hand. A 23-second <a href="/media/app-preview.mp4">screen recording of 1.4 on iPhone</a> is available for embedding or broadcast.</p>

    <p class="small"><a href={appStoreUrl('web-press')}>Inkline on the App Store</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
